.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_CREATE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_create
.Nd create a new file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_create "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "const char *name" "mode_t mode" "struct ucred *cred"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_create
function creates a new regular file named
.Fa name
in the directory
.Fa dvp .
If successful, the new vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The directory vnode where the file will be created.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the new vnode will be stored.
.It Fa name
The name of the new file.
.It Fa mode
The mode (permissions) for the new file.
.It Fa cred
The user credentials for the operation.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er ENOTDIR"
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The vnode
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
The file already exists.
.It Bq Er EACCES
Permission denied.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_mkdir 9 ,
.Xr vop_mknod 9
